+### ADR-114, Amendment 51 (21 November 2026) — a release also attaches its maintainer's manifest, signed as the lock is — Accepted by the owner, 21 November 2026
+
+Status: **Accepted by the owner, 21 November 2026**, in his ruling on build RL1. It adds to decision 4 ("a release is its `versions.lock`")
+and decision 11 (the lock is signed). **A release also attaches a maintainer's manifest of the tag: a CSV with one row per tracked file of the
+product tree and a short summary with one row per folder, both generated by `OspreyFlow_Core/scripts/maintainer_manifest.py` from the tracked files at the
+tag and signed keyless beside the lock; they are not read by `update` and a release is not refused for lacking them.** The files carry no
+"maintained under" column, which is written only when a second rules file is supplied on the command line and none is supplied by the
+release.
+
+Tests that would fail (rule 12): the manifest test (slice RL1: the same ref gives the same bytes; a tracked file under `apps`, `packages`
+or `services` that falls in no area, or in two, fails; the release's default output has no "maintained under" column).
